{"type": "answer", "run_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "overload_naive_retry", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q4", "request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0009", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:10.349+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 29.007, "patience_s": 14.2, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 6336.6, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0009", "question": "Per Table 1, how does self-attention compare with recurrent layers on complexity per layer, sequential operations and maximum path length?", "kind": "passages", "level": 3, "text": "No written answer this time: here are the most relevant passages from the papers, quoted as they are. A written answer should be possible in about 1 s.\n[S1] 1706.03762v7 pp.6-7 §4: \"The shorter these paths between any combination of positions in the input and output sequences, the easier it is to learn long-range dependencies [12]. Hence we also compare the maximum path length between any two input and output positions in networks composed of the different layer types. As noted in Table 1, a self-attention layer connects all positions with a constant number of sequentially executed operations, whereas a recurrent layer requires O(n) sequential operations.\"\n[S2] 1706.03762v7 pp.5-6 §3.4: \"In the embedding layers, we multiply those weights by √ d_model. Table 1: Maximum path lengths, per-layer complexity and minimum number of sequential operations for different layer types. n is the sequence length, d is the representation dimension, k is the kernel size of convolutions and r the size of the neighborhood in restricted self-attention. Layer Type Complexity per Layer Sequential Maximum Path Length Operations Self-Attention O(n^2 · d) O(1) O(1) Recurrent O(n · d^2) O(n) O(n) Convolutional O(k · n · d^2) O(1) O(log_k(n)) Self-Attention (restricted) O(r · n · d) O(1) O(n/r)\"", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "1706.03762v7 pp.6-7 §4", "pid": "attention:2400:0012", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p06-b011", "attention-p06-b012", "attention-p06-b013", "attention-p06-b014", "attention-p07-b001"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "1706.03762v7 pp.5-6 §3.4", "pid": "attention:2400:0010", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p05-b017", "attention-p05-b018", "attention-p06-b001", "attention-p06-b002"]}], "notice": "passages only, no model call: no drafter available (openai/gpt-oss-120b: 429 rate_limited)", "eta_s": 0.0, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 249, "completion_tokens": 62}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 0.8, "model": null, "outcome": "full", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 0.0}}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b"}}, {"name": "understand", "start_ms": 0.8, "end_ms": 280.3, "model": null, "outcome": "router", "detail": {}}, {"name": "wait:understand", "start_ms": 0.8, "end_ms": 0.8, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:understand", "start_ms": 0.8, "end_ms": 280.3, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "200:ok", "detail": {}}, {"name": "retrieve", "start_ms": 280.4, "end_ms": 280.7, "model": null, "outcome": "1 search", "detail": {"query": "Table 1 self-attention recurrent cost per layer sequential operations longest dependency path Per Table 1, how does self-attention compare with recurrent layers on complexity per layer, sequential operations and maximum path length?", "papers": ["attention"], "k": 3, "evidence": {"best": 1.0, "union": 1.0, "top_bm25": 82.609, "query_terms": 13}}}, {"name": "decide", "start_ms": 280.7, "end_ms": 280.8, "model": null, "outcome": "draft", "detail": {"best": 1.0, "union": 1.0, "top_bm25": 82.609, "query_terms": 13}}, {"name": "draft", "start_ms": 280.8, "end_ms": 6334.8, "model": null, "outcome": "error:_Step", "detail": {"level": "full"}}, {"name": "wait:draft", "start_ms": 280.8, "end_ms": 280.8, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:draft", "start_ms": 280.8, "end_ms": 3321.1, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "outcome": "429:rate_limited", "detail": {}}, {"name": "wait:draft", "start_ms": 3321.1, "end_ms": 3321.1, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:draft", "start_ms": 3321.1, "end_ms": 6334.8, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "outcome": "429:rate_limited", "detail": {}}, {"name": "send", "start_ms": 6336.5, "end_ms": 6336.5, "model": null, "outcome": "passages", "detail": {}}], "checks": {"router": {"papers": ["attention"], "query": "Table 1 self-attention recurrent cost per layer sequential operations longest dependency path Per Table 1, how does self-attention compare with recurrent layers on complexity per layer, sequential operations and maximum path length?", "alt_query": "complexity comparison linear versus quadratic operations recurrence depth Per Table 1, how does self-attention compare with recurrent layers on complexity per layer, sequential operations and maximum path length?"}, "retrieval": {"query": "Table 1 self-attention recurrent cost per layer sequential operations longest dependency path Per Table 1, how does self-attention compare with recurrent layers on complexity per layer, sequential operations and maximum path length?", "papers": ["attention"], "k": 3, "pids": ["attention:2400:0012", "attention:2400:0010", "attention:2400:0013"]}}, "released_ms": 6336.5, "budget_wait_ms": 0.0, "tokens_in": 249, "tokens_out": 62, "level_name": "passages", "pipeline_model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 249, "completion_tokens": 62, "tokens_estimated": false, "ms": 279.3969999984256, "waited_s": 0.0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0, "tokens_estimated": true, "ms": 1.1832999953185208, "waited_s": 0.0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0, "tokens_estimated": true, "ms": 1.3256999955046922, "waited_s": 0.0}]}}
{"type": "answer", "run_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "overload_naive_retry", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q13", "request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0010", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:12.108+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 30.783, "patience_s": 44.99, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 6305.3, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0010", "question": "In H-Net, what do the encoder and decoder networks do, and at what resolution do they run?", "kind": "passages", "level": 3, "text": "No written answer this time: here are the most relevant passages from the papers, quoted as they are. A written answer should be possible in about 1 s.\n[S1] 2507.07955v2 pp.19-20 §3.3: \"A natural question arises: does the importance of Mamba layers (i) stem specifically from processing fine-grained byte inputs, or (ii) because they are better for compressing information into the next stage, even at coarser input resolutions? To investigate these hypotheses, we train a 1-stage H-Net on top of BPE-tokenized inputs processed by the GPT-2 tokenizer. We then evaluate six different encoder-decoder combinations.\"\n[S2] 2507.07955v2 p.2 §1: \"Hierarchical Processing. The H-Net adopts the hierarchical architecture from prior work (Goel et al. 2022; Nawrot, Tworkowski, et al. 2022; Slagle 2024), resembling an autoregressive U-Net (Ronneberger, Fischer, and Brox 2015): (i) raw data is processed by a small encoder network, (ii) then downsampled and passed through a main network operating on compressed chunks, (iii) and finally upsampled before being passed through a decoder network operating on the original resolution.\"", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "2507.07955v2 pp.19-20 §3.3", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:2400:0035", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p19-b005", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b006", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b007", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b008", "dynamic_chunking-p19-b009", "dynamic_chunking-p20-b001"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "2507.07955v2 p.2 §1", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:2400:0003", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p02-b008", "dynamic_chunking-p02-b009", "dynamic_chunking-p02-b010"]}], "notice": "passages only, no model call: no drafter available (openai/gpt-oss-120b: 429 rate_limited)", "eta_s": 0.0, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 239, "completion_tokens": 50}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 0.5, "model": null, "outcome": "full", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 0.0}}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b"}}, {"name": "understand", "start_ms": 0.5, "end_ms": 234.0, "model":