{"type": "answer", "run_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "overload_naive_retry", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q3", "request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0016", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:50.391+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 69.057, "patience_s": 53.66, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 6418.6, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0016", "question": "How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?", "kind": "passages", "level": 3, "text": "No written answer this time: here are the most relevant passages from the papers, quoted as they are. A written answer should be possible in about 1 s.\n[S1] 1706.03762v7 p.6 §3.5: \"To this end, we add \"positional encodings\" to the input embeddings at the bottoms of the encoder and decoder stacks. The positional encodings have the same dimension d_model as the embeddings, so that the two can be summed. There are many choices of positional encodings, learned and fixed [9]. In this work, we use sine and cosine functions of different frequencies: P E_(pos,2i) = sin(pos/10000^2i/d_model) P E_(pos,2i+1) = cos(pos/10000^2i/d_model) where pos is the position and i is the dimension. That is, each dimension of the positional encoding corresponds to a sinusoid.\"\n[S2] 1706.03762v7 pp.8-9 §6.2: \"In Table 3 rows (B), we observe that reducing the attention key size d_k hurts model quality. This suggests that determining compatibility is not easy and that a more sophisticated compatibility function than dot product may be beneficial. We further observe in rows (C) and (D) that, as expected, bigger models are better, and dropout is very helpful in avoiding over-fitting. In row (E) we replace our sinusoidal positional encoding with learned positional embeddings [9], and observe nearly identical results to the base model.\"", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "1706.03762v7 p.6 §3.5", "pid": "attention:2400:0011", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p06-b004", "attention-p06-b005", "attention-p06-b006", "attention-p06-b007", "attention-p06-b008", "attention-p06-b009"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "1706.03762v7 pp.8-9 §6.2", "pid": "attention:2400:0020", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p08-b012", "attention-p08-b013", "attention-p09-b001", "attention-p09-b002", "attention-p09-b003", "attention-p09-b004", "attention-p09-b005"]}], "notice": "passages only, no model call: no drafter available (openai/gpt-oss-120b: 429 rate_limited)", "eta_s": 0.0, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 239, "completion_tokens": 56}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 0.7, "model": null, "outcome": "full", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 0.0}}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b"}}, {"name": "understand", "start_ms": 0.8, "end_ms": 381.0, "model": null, "outcome": "router", "detail": {}}, {"name": "wait:understand", "start_ms": 0.8, "end_ms": 0.8, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:understand", "start_ms": 0.8, "end_ms": 380.9, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "200:ok", "detail": {}}, {"name": "retrieve", "start_ms": 381.0, "end_ms": 381.2, "model": null, "outcome": "1 search", "detail": {"query": "sinusoidal positional encoding formula absolute position relative ordering property How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?", "papers": ["attention"], "k": 3, "evidence": {"best": 0.719, "union": 0.719, "top_bm25": 56.081, "query_terms": 7}}}, {"name": "decide", "start_ms": 381.2, "end_ms": 381.3, "model": null, "outcome": "draft", "detail": {"best": 0.719, "union": 0.719, "top_bm25": 56.081, "query_terms": 7}}, {"name": "draft", "start_ms": 381.3, "end_ms": 6416.6, "model": null, "outcome": "error:_Step", "detail": {"level": "full"}}, {"name": "wait:draft", "start_ms": 381.3, "end_ms": 381.3, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:draft", "start_ms": 381.3, "end_ms": 3402.4, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "outcome": "429:rate_limited", "detail": {}}, {"name": "wait:draft", "start_ms": 3402.5, "end_ms": 3402.5, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:draft", "start_ms": 3402.5, "end_ms": 6416.6, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "outcome": "429:rate_limited", "detail": {}}, {"name": "send", "start_ms": 6418.4, "end_ms": 6418.4, "model": null, "outcome": "passages", "detail": {}}], "checks": {"router": {"papers": ["attention"], "query": "sinusoidal positional encoding formula absolute position relative ordering property How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?", "alt_query": "learned position embeddings addition input position information How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?"}, "retrieval": {"query": "sinusoidal positional encoding formula absolute position relative ordering property How are the positional encodings built, and why sinusoids rather than learned embeddings?", "papers": ["attention"], "k": 3, "pids": ["attention:2400:0011", "attention:2400:0020", "attention:2400:0018"]}}, "released_ms": 6418.4, "budget_wait_ms": 0.0, "tokens_in": 239, "tokens_out": 56, "level_name": "passages", "pipeline_model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 239, "completion_tokens": 56, "tokens_estimated": false, "ms": 380.0810000029742, "waited_s": 0.0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0, "tokens_estimated": true, "ms": 0.9104999990086071, "waited_s": 0.0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0, "tokens_estimated": true, "ms": 0.9208999981638044, "waited_s": 0.0}]}}
{"type": "answer", "run_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "overload_naive_retry", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q1", "request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0017", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:54.315+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 72.985, "patience_s": 24.51, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 5091.6, "degraded": false, "reply": {"request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0017", "question": "In simple terms, what does scaled dot-product attention compute, and why divide the query-key dot products by sqrt(d_k)?", "kind": "answer", "level": 0, "text": "In simple terms, scaled dot-product attention computes a weighted sum of input values, where the weight for each value is determined by the compatibility between a query and its corresponding key [S2]. This compatibility is measured by calculating the dot product of the query vector with all key vectors [S1]. The raw dot products are then divided by the square root of the query and key dimension, denoted as $d_k$, and a softmax function is applied to these scaled scores to generate the final attention weights [S1]. Dividing by $\\sqrt{d_k}$ is necessary to prevent the dot products from becoming too large in magnitude when the dimensionality is high [S1]. If the dot products grow too large, it pushes the softmax function into regions where it has extremely small gradients, which hinders effective learning [S1]. This scaling ensures that the attention mechanism remains stable and efficient during training for larger values of $d_k$ [S1].", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "1706.03762v7 p.4 §3.2.1", "pid": "attention:2400:0006", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p04-b005", "attention-p04-b006", "attention-p04-b007", "attention-p04-b008", "attention-p04-b009", "attention-p04-b010", "attention-p04-b011", "attention-p04-b012", "attention-p04-b013"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "1706.03762v7 pp.3-4 §3.2", "pid": "attention:2400:0005", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p03-b007", "attention-p04-b001", "attention-p04-b002", "attention-p04-b003"]}, {"sid": "S3", "cite": "1706.03762v7 pp.4-5 §3.2.2", "pid": "attention:2400:0007", "paper": "attention", "block_ids": ["attention-p04-b015", "attention-p04-b016", "attention-p04-b017", "attention-p05-b001", "attention-p05-b002", "attention-p05-b003", "attention-p05-b004", "attention-p05-b005", "attention-p05-b006"]}], "notice": "", "eta_s": null, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 246, "completion_tokens": 69}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 1038, "completion_tokens": 311}, {"step": "verify", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 1139, "completion_tokens": 6}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 0.7, "model": null, "outcome": "full", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 0.0}}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b"}}, {"name": "understand", "start_ms": 0.7, "end_ms": 343.4, "model": null, "outcome": "router", "detail": {}}, {"name": "wait:understand", "start_ms": 0.7, "end_ms": 0.8, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:understand", "start_ms": 0.8, "end_ms": 343.4, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "200:ok", "detail": {}}, {"name": "retrieve", "start_ms": 343.4, "end_ms": 343.7, "model": null, "outcome": "1 search", "detail": {"query": "scaled dot-product attention temperature d_k softmax probability distribution vanishing gradients In simple terms, what does scaled dot-product attention compute, and why divide the query-key dot products by sqrt(d_k)?", "papers": ["attention"], "k": 3, "evidence": {"best": 0.832, "union": 0.832, "top_bm25": 87.907, "query_terms": 13}}}, {"name": "decide", "start_ms": 343.7, "end_ms": 343.8, "model": null, "outcome": "draft", "detail": {"best": 0.832, "union": 0.832, "top_bm25": 87.907, "query_terms": 13}}, {"name": "draft", "start_ms": 343.8, "end_ms": 4917.1, "model": null, "outcome": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "detail": {"level": "full"}}, {"name": "wait:draft", "start_ms": 343.8, "end_ms": 343.8, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:draft", "start_ms": 343.9, "end_ms": 4917.1, "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "outcome": "200:ok", "detail": {}}, {"name": "check", "start_ms": 4917.2, "end_ms": 5091.2, "model": null, "outcome": "pass", "detail": {"gate_ok": true, "failures": 0, "verifier": {"ok": true, "unsupported": [], "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"}}}, {"name": "verify", "start_ms": 4917.9, "end_ms": 5091.1, "model": null, "outcome": "pass", "detail": {}}, {"name": "wait:verify", "start_ms": 4917.9, "end_ms": 4917.9, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "granted", "detail": {"waited_s": 0.0}}, {"name": "call:verify", "start_ms": 4917.9, "end_ms": 5091.1, "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "outcome": "200:ok", "detail": {}}, {"name": "send", "start_ms": 5091.2, "end_ms": 5091.2, "model": null, "outcome": "answer", "detail": {}}], "checks": {"gate": {"ok": true, "sentences": 6, "failures": []}, "verifier": {"ok": true, "unsupported": [], "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b"}, "draft_model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "attempts": 1, "router": {"papers": ["attention"], "query": "scaled dot-product attention temperature d_k softmax probability distribution vanishing gradients In simple terms, what does scaled dot-product attention compute, and why divide the query-key dot products by sqrt(d_k)?", "alt_query": "rescaling attention scores prevent saturation deep in backpropagation high magnitude dot products In simple terms, what does scaled dot-product attention compute, and why divide the query-key dot products by sqrt(d_k)?"}, "retrieval": {"query": "scaled dot-product attention temperature d_k softmax probability distribution vanishing gradients In simple terms, what does scaled dot-product attention compute, and why divide the query-key dot products by sqrt(d_k)?", "papers": ["attention"], "k": 3, "pids": ["attention:2400:0006", "attention:2400:0005", "attention:2400:0007"]}}, "released_ms": 5091.2, "budget_wait_ms": 0.1, "tokens_in": 2423, "tokens_out": 386, "level_name": "full", "pipeline_model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 246, "completion_tokens": 69, "tokens_estimated": false, "ms": 342.54279999731807, "waited_s": 0.0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 1038, "completion_tokens": 311, "tokens_estimated": false, "ms": 4573.124999995343, "waited_s": 0.0}, {"step": "verify", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 1139, "completion_tokens": 6, "tokens_estimated": false, "ms": 173.09920000116108, "waited_s": 0.0}]}}
{"type": "answer", "run_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "overload_naive_retry", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q8", "request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0018", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:32:55.071+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 73.751, "patience_s": 17.49, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 6341.4, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0018", "question": "What are Moshi's main components and what does each do?", "kind": "passages", "level": 3, "text": "No written answer this time: here are the most relevant passages from the papers, quoted as they are. A written answer should be possible in about 1 s.\n[S1] 2410.00037v1 pp.6-7 §3.1: \"To jointly model the audio streams from Moshi and the user, as well as Moshi’s text tokens, we rely on a Depth Transformer compatible with streaming inference (Sections 3.4.1, 3.4.2). In this section, we further detail each of these components. We then describe the training datasets and the different training phases we used to train Moshi in Section 4. Finally, in Section 5, we report thorough evaluation results on Moshi’s abilities, both linguistic and acoustic, as well as ablation experiments on its main components, while Section 6 provides analyses on the safety of our system.\"\n[S2] 2410.00037v1 p.6 §2: \"Figure 1: Overview of Moshi . Moshi is a speech-text foundation model which enables real-time spoken dialogue. The main components of Moshi’s architecture are: a bespoke text language model backbone (Helium, see Section 3.2); a neural audio codec with residual vector quantization and with semantic knowledge distilled from a self-supervised speech model (Mimi, Section 3.3); the streaming, hierarchical generation of semantic and acoustic tokens for both the user and Moshi, along with time-aligned text tokens for Moshi when using Inner Monologue (Section 3.4). been proposed by Wang et al.\"", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "2410.00037v1 pp.6-7 §3.1", "pid": "moshi:2400:0009", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p06-b005", "moshi-p07-b001", "moshi-p07-b002"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "2410.00037v1 p.6 §2", "pid": "moshi:2400:0008", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p06-b001", "moshi-p06-b002"]}], "notice": "passages only, no model call: no drafter available (openai/gpt-oss-120b: 429 rate_limited)", "eta_s": 0.0, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 231, "completion_tokens": 82}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 1.2, "model": null, "outcome": "full", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 0.0}}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b"}}, {"name": "understand", "start_ms": 1.2, "end_ms":