{"type": "answer", "run_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "overload_naive_retry", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q18", "request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0021", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:33:08.901+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 87.566, "patience_s": 10.7, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 6374.3, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0021", "question": "How much energy (kWh) or CO2 did training the H-Net models use?", "kind": "passages", "level": 3, "text": "No written answer this time: here are the most relevant passages from the papers, quoted as they are. A written answer should be possible in about 1 s.\n[S1] 2507.07955v2 p.12 §3.1: \"Training Curves. Figure 3 presents validation BPB metrics throughout training for both Large and XL model scales. Large Scale. At the Large scale, we make note of the following comparisons. • All isotropic models severely underperform hierarchical models. Among these, MambaByte is significantly better than LlamaByte, both the FLOP-matched sliding window attention (SWA) variant and even the global attention variant that is data-matched but uses 2× the FLOPs. • H-Net (pool) is much worse than all other H-Net variants, validating that fixed-width chunking is not effective.\"\n[S2] 2507.07955v2 p.5 §2.1.2: \"Our ablation studies (Section 3.3) confirm that SSM-based encoders/decoders significantly outperform Transformer layers, not just at the byte level but even on coarser inputs, which we attribute to their stronger inductive bias for compression which helps build abstractions (Gu 2025). Main Network. H-Net’s computational efficiency stems from strategic parameter allocation. We concentrate the majority of model capacity in the main network, which operates on progressively compressed sequences.\"", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "2507.07955v2 p.12 §3.1", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:2400:0024", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p12-b003", "dynamic_chunking-p12-b004", "dynamic_chunking-p12-b005", "dynamic_chunking-p12-b006", "dynamic_chunking-p12-b007", "dynamic_chunking-p12-b008", "dynamic_chunking-p12-b009", "dynamic_chunking-p12-b010", "dynamic_chunking-p12-b011", "dynamic_chunking-p12-b012"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "2507.07955v2 p.5 §2.1.2", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:2400:0008", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p05-b011", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b012", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b013", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b014"]}], "notice": "passages only, no model call: no drafter available (openai/gpt-oss-120b: 429 rate_limited)", "eta_s": 0.0, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 233, "completion_tokens": 60}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completi