{"type": "answer", "run_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z", "scenario": "overload_naive_retry", "source": "stand-in", "setting": "large", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 2400, "k": 3, "rerank": false, "router": true}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q17", "request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0029", "start_time": "2026-11-10T18:33:45.767+00:00", "arrival_offset_s": 124.431, "patience_s": 32.25, "gave_up": false, "waited_ms": 6291.8, "degraded": true, "reply": {"request_id": "overload_naive_retry-20261110T183141Z-0029", "question": "What is H-Net's p95 latency serving 1,000 simultaneous requests?", "kind": "passages", "level": 3, "text": "No written answer this time: here are the most relevant passages from the papers, quoted as they are. A written answer should be possible in about 1 s.\n[S1] 2507.07955v2 p.5 §2.1.2: \"Encoder and Decoder Networks. The encoder and decoder networks in H-Net face unique design constraints due to their dual objectives and computational requirements. Each encoder must simultaneously (i) preserve fine-grained information for transmission to its corresponding decoder through residual connections (3), and (ii) compress inputs into chunks of richer representations for the main network. The decoder, in turn, must effectively combine coarse-grained representations from the main network with fine-grained details from the encoder residuals.\"\n[S2] 2410.00037v1 p.2 §1: \"Voice has provided a convenient interface to early conversational systems, from Alexa^1 to Siri^2 and Google Assistant.^3 In this context, a “wake word” spoken by the user typically triggers an automatic speech recognition (ASR) system which transcribes the subsequent user’s request. Then, a natural language understanding (NLU) pipeline converts this query to a structured format used to produce a text answer through natural language generation (NLG). Eventually, a text-to-speech (TTS) system tells the answer back to the user. While this process can handle short, constrained interactions (e.g.\"", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "2507.07955v2 p.5 §2.1.2", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:2400:0008", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p05-b011", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b012", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b013", "dynamic_chunking-p05-b014"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "2410.00037v1 p.2 §1", "pid": "moshi:2400:0001", "paper": "moshi", "block_ids": ["moshi-p02-b002", "moshi-p02-b003"]}], "notice": "passages only, no model call: no drafter available (openai/gpt-oss-120b: 429 rate_limited)", "eta_s": 0.0, "model_calls": [{"step": "understand", "model": "qwen/qwen3.8-27b", "status": 200, "outcome": "ok", "prompt_tokens": 233, "completion_tokens": 43}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}, {"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 429, "outcome": "rate_limited", "prompt_tokens": 0, "completion_tokens": 0}], "spans": [{"name": "plan", "start_ms": 0.0, "end_ms": 0.7, "model": null, "outcome": "full", "detail": {"predicted_wait_s": {"full": {"openai/gpt-oss-120b": 0.0}}, "drafter": "openai